# alarm-sigalrm-disposition.baseline
#
# Grandfathered list of alarm() callsites in fork()-containing files
# that trip the heuristic in
# scripts/check-static/alarm-sigalrm-disposition.sh but which are in
# fact legitimate -- the alarm() call is in the long-lived trinity child
# process itself (not in a forked grandchild), or is an alarm(0)/restore
# call rather than a watchdog arming.
#
# Format: `path/to/file.c:lineno  reason text...`
# Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored.
#
# This baseline should SHRINK over time as false positives are
# resolved via narrower detection.  A new alarm() arming in a
# forked grandchild body without signal(SIGALRM, SIG_DFL) must FAIL
# the gate, never be silently added here.

# child/child.c: alarm(0) cancel and alarm(1) re-arm calls in the
# long-lived trinity dispatch child.  The SIGALRM flag-setter is the
# *intended* handler for these calls (they power the per-syscall
# timeout); no SIG_DFL reset is wanted.
child/child.c:361  alarm(0) cancel in dispatch loop -- parent scope, flag-setter is correct
child/child.c:525  alarm(1) re-arm in dispatch loop -- parent scope, flag-setter is correct
child/child.c:921  alarm(0) cancel in dispatch loop -- parent scope, flag-setter is correct

# dispatch/syscall-exec.c: alarm(1) watchdog and alarm(0) cancel in the
# exec-dispatch path, executed in the long-lived child process, not a
# forked grandchild.  Flag-setter is the intended handler here.
dispatch/syscall-exec.c:388  alarm(1) exec watchdog -- parent scope, flag-setter is correct
dispatch/syscall-exec.c:493  alarm(0) cancel -- parent scope, flag-setter is correct

# lib/userns-bootstrap.c: these three alarm() calls are in
# userns_run_in_ns(), the PARENT side of the grandchild fork.  The
# grandchild's alarm (line ~191) already has the signal(SIGALRM, SIG_DFL)
# fix applied (commit fdb73bc89fe4).  The parent calls here are:
#   241: alarm(USERNS_PARENT_ALARM_S) -- cap wait time in parent
#   243: alarm(rem) restore on waitpid error
#   246: alarm(rem) restore after waitpid success
# All three are in the parent where the flag-setter is correct.
lib/userns-bootstrap.c:266  parent-side alarm arm in userns_run_in_ns -- not a grandchild body
lib/userns-bootstrap.c:268  parent-side alarm(rem) restore on error path
lib/userns-bootstrap.c:271  parent-side alarm(rem) restore after waitpid
